Avaritia Integration

Purpose

Avaritia represents the final progression system of the pack.

It exists beyond conventional industrial technology, advanced magic, ProjectE, and normal endgame automation.

Avaritia should provide the ultimate crafting objectives of the pack.

Its purpose is not to introduce another ordinary technology tier.

Its purpose is to give the player extremely demanding final objectives that require the combined infrastructure of the entire pack.

Role in the Pack

Avaritia is responsible for:

Extreme Crafting

Neutronium progression

Infinity progression

Extreme resource requirements

Final equipment

Ultimate crafting objectives

Final progression milestones

Avaritia should represent the absolute end of the progression.

Avaritia Unlock

Avaritia should remain inaccessible until the player has completed the major post-endgame systems.

The Avaritia unlock should require substantial progress through:

UHV

Post-Endgame

Advanced automation

Magic progression

Apotheosis progression

ProjectE

Extreme resource production

Cross-mod infrastructure

The player should already have access to ProjectE before beginning the main Avaritia progression.

Avaritia should be the final destination rather than another intermediate system.

Avaritia Progression

Avaritia should have multiple stages.

Initial Avaritia

The player gains access to Extreme Crafting and begins producing the materials required for advanced Avaritia components.

Neutronium Stage

The player begins large-scale Neutronium production.

Advanced Avaritia

The player begins producing increasingly complex components using Neutronium and other endgame materials.

Infinity Stage

The player begins producing Infinity components and the most demanding Avaritia items.

Final Stage

The player completes the ultimate crafting objectives of the pack.

Extreme Crafting

Extreme Crafting should be one of the defining mechanics of the final progression.

Extreme Crafting recipes should require enormous quantities of carefully selected resources.

Recipes should combine:

GregTech materials

Modern Industrialization materials

Mekanism materials

AE2 components

Create components

Magical materials

Exploration resources

Apotheosis materials

ProjectE infrastructure

Neutronium

Infinity components

Extreme Crafting recipes should represent actual progression milestones.

They should not simply multiply existing recipe costs without purpose.

GregTech Integration

GregTech should provide a large portion of the industrial foundation required for Avaritia.

UHV materials and infrastructure should be required for early Avaritia progression.

Advanced GregTech materials may become components of Neutronium and Infinity production.

Modern Industrialization Integration

Modern Industrialization should contribute advanced industrial materials and processing systems.

Its endgame machinery may be required to produce components used in Avaritia recipes.

Mekanism Integration

Mekanism should contribute advanced chemical processing and high-throughput industrial infrastructure.

Late-game Mekanism systems may be required for the production of specific Avaritia components.

Applied Energistics 2 Integration

AE2 should become extremely important for managing Avaritia production.

Avaritia recipes should require enormous quantities of materials.

Advanced ME systems should therefore be useful for:

Resource storage

Automated crafting

Production logistics

Intermediate component management

Large-scale resource routing

AE2 should manage the complexity of Avaritia without removing the difficulty of producing the required resources.

Create Integration

Create should remain useful for physical logistics and specialized production infrastructure.

Large-scale material movement may use:

Mechanical belts

Funnels

Contraptions

Trains

Mechanical processing

Create should remain relevant even at the final stage of the pack.

Magic Integration

Advanced magical resources should contribute to Avaritia progression.

Some final components may require:

Rare magical materials

Endgame rituals

Magical resources

Advanced magical infrastructure

Magic should therefore remain relevant until the final stages.

Apotheosis Integration

Apotheosis may provide final equipment components, rare boss materials, or other advanced resources.

High-level Apotheosis progression should be substantially completed before the final Avaritia milestones.

ProjectE Integration

ProjectE should be an important prerequisite for large-scale Avaritia production.

ProjectE provides the resource manipulation necessary to support extreme production requirements.

However, ProjectE should not trivialize Avaritia.

The most important Avaritia materials should have controlled EMC values.

Some Avaritia resources may intentionally have extremely low or carefully restricted EMC values.

Neutronium Progression

Neutronium should be one of the first major Avaritia production milestones.

Neutronium production should require substantial post-endgame infrastructure.

The player should need:

Large-scale resource generation

Extreme automation

Advanced power infrastructure

ProjectE systems

Large storage capacity

High-throughput production

Neutronium should not be immediately obtainable after unlocking Avaritia.

Infinity Progression

Infinity should represent the final material progression.

Its production should require enormous quantities of advanced resources and Neutronium.

Infinity components should require multiple stages of production.

Infinity should be intentionally difficult to produce even with ProjectE.

The player should need a fully developed post-endgame infrastructure.

Final Equipment

Avaritia equipment should represent the strongest equipment available in the pack.

Access to final equipment should require completion of the appropriate Avaritia progression.

Equipment should not become available through alternative recipes or unintended crafting methods.

The final equipment should represent the completion of the technological, magical, and industrial progression.

Final Crafting Goals

The pack should contain several extreme crafting objectives.

Possible objectives include:

Ultimate industrial components

Extreme automation components

Advanced magical components

Neutronium-based components

Infinity-based components

Final equipment

Ultimate crafting items

The objectives should require different parts of the pack rather than only one production chain.

Final Progression Milestone

The final progression milestone should require completion of the ultimate Avaritia objectives.

The player should demonstrate mastery of:

GregTech

Modern Industrialization

Create

Mekanism

Applied Energistics 2

Create Aeronautics

Create Big Cannons

Magic

Apotheosis

ProjectE

Avaritia

The final milestone should not be achievable by focusing exclusively on one system.

Avaritia Quests

Avaritia should have a dedicated final quest chapter.

The chapter should introduce:

Avaritia

Extreme Crafting

Neutronium

Advanced components

Infinity

Final equipment

Ultimate crafting objectives

Final progression milestones

The final quests should be extremely demanding.

Quest rewards should be mostly informational, cosmetic, or progression-supporting rather than resources that trivialize the next objective.

GuideME Integration

GuideME should contain complete documentation for the Avaritia progression.

Documentation should explain:

Extreme Crafting

Avaritia materials

Neutronium

Infinity

Production requirements

Cross-mod dependencies

ProjectE interaction

Final crafting objectives

The handbook should clearly communicate that Avaritia represents the final progression of the pack.

Final Automation

Avaritia should require the player to automate production on an extreme scale.

Manual crafting should become impractical.

The intended solution should be:

Massive resource production

ProjectE automation

AE2 logistics

Industrial processing

Parallel production lines

Large-scale power infrastructure

Automated intermediate components

The final challenge should therefore be infrastructure rather than repetitive clicking.

Final Milestone

The final milestone is achieved when the player completes the ultimate Avaritia objectives and obtains the final items defined by the pack.

Completion should represent the culmination of the entire progression.

There should be no ordinary technological tier after Avaritia.

Avaritia is the final technological destination.

Post-Avaritia Content

Although Avaritia represents the end of the progression, the world should remain open.

Players may continue building:

Larger factories

More efficient automation

Additional resource infrastructure

Massive AE2 networks

Extreme Create machines

Additional exploration infrastructure

Experimental systems

Post-Avaritia construction should be optional and should not represent another required progression tier.

Final Goal

Avaritia should make the player look back at the entire progression and recognize that every previous system contributed to the final result.

The player begins with basic survival.

They progress through primitive industry, steam, electrical technology, advanced automation, magic, exploration, and post-endgame systems.

ProjectE provides extreme resource manipulation.

Avaritia then asks the player to use everything they have built to accomplish the final objectives.

Avaritia is not simply the most expensive crafting system.

It is the final examination of the entire pack.
